<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">In Greek mythology, the Argo was the ship on which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jason">Jason</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argonauts">Argonauts</a> sailed from Iolkos in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> to Colchis on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> in search of the Golden Fleece. It was said to have been built by Argus with the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a> and to carry a speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> from the oak of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodona">Dodona</a>. The voyage was told most fully in the Argonautica of Apollonius of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argo.jpg" alt="Argo" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Konstantinos Volanakis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Constantine_Volanakis_Argo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
